From 21d1fa8d86111256be723a4fb82b526ed18ce14b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: murdoa <murdoa@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:05:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Add the m6809-none-elf and m6800-none-elf targets

Both drive the LLVM M6809 and M6800 backends: 16-bit pointers and int,
big-endian, byte-aligned, no atomics, panic=abort. The C calling
convention matches clang: aggregates are passed byval and returned
through a hidden pointer, and small integers are extended to 16 bits.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
